1958 and 1960.  It seemed possible that the US oligarchy in Olympic basketball might be threatened."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The US chose an all-star team for its 1960 Olympic team, rather than selecting players from a winning team.  The team they chose is often considered the greatest amateur basketball team of all-time.  It was led by guards " [:a {:href "/athletes/6970"} "Oscar Robertson"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/7351"} "Jerry West"] ", who thru the 1980s, until the advent of " [:a {:href "/athletes/6342"} "Michael Jordan"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/6336"} "Magic Johnson"] ", were often considered the two finest guards in basketball history.  Other future NBA stars on the team included " [:a {:href "/athletes/6557"} "Jerry Lucas"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/6014"} "Terry Dischinger"] " (both later NBA rookies-of-the-year), and center " [:a {:href "/athletes/5704"} "Walt Bellamy"] ".  The team was so strong that future NBA star John Havlicek was chosen only as an alternate."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the Olympic tournament, the United States defeated its three main rivals easily – Brazil by 27 points in the final game, the USSR by 24 points in preliminary competition, and Italy by 31 points in the final pool.  The game against the Soviet Union was the closest match they had in the tournament.  Through five Olympic tournaments, the United States had still not lost a game."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button313461", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button313461').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Scoring Average"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Disqualifications"] [:th {:style "display: none",